<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Plan 53 §3.4's cycle-record bullet for mode B, and its G3: under
  `takes-split`, a clip that STARTS INSIDE the cycle gives TWO COLUMNS PER
  CYCLE, and no take reaches beyond the cycle. "B — two columns per cycle when
  a clip starts inside it (G3), accepted."

  Driven through `place-recording mode="takes-split"` directly, once per pass,
  which is exactly how the recorder submits a cycle: §3.4 says "every pass is
  one span [cycleIn, cycleOut) against the lane as the previous pass left it",
  and this case is that sentence with the transport taken out of it. So every
  number is arithmetic and the two passes are identical by construction rather
  than by luck — a real cycle's passes differ by capture jitter, which is what
  makes `record_loop_takes` a floor-assertion case and this one an exact one.

  GEOMETRY. test_sawtooth.wav is 192000 frames (4 s at 48 kHz):

      cycle = [96000, 144000)      the span of every pass
      O     = [120000, 192000)     a clip STARTING INSIDE the cycle

  PASS 1 cuts O at the cycle end and fills the part of the cycle O does not
  cover, leaving

      child 0   [120000, 144000)   column: take 0 = O's head, take 1 = pass 1
      child 1   [96000,  120000)   the plain cut for the uncovered part
      child 2   [144000, 192000)   O's tail, OUTSIDE the cycle, srcOffset 24000

  PASS 2 then touches children 0 and 1 — both lie inside the cycle, neither
  needs cutting — and adds a take to each:

      child 0   3 takes, pass 2 active
      child 1   2 takes, pass 2 active
      child 2   untouched

  TWO COLUMNS, ONE CYCLE. That is G3, and it is the accepted cost of mode B:
  mode A would have made ONE union column per cycle instead. Index order is
  insertion order, so the column that sounds SECOND is child 0 and the one
  that sounds first is child 1.

  NO TAKE BEYOND THE CYCLE, which is X8 narrowed (§3.1 step 5), and child 2 is
  where it is checked: it keeps its own extent [144000,192000) and never
  becomes a take of anything. A planner that let a pass spill past `b` would
  have swallowed it.

  THE TAKE ANCHORS ARE ASSERTED, and with a deliberate wrong value rejected
  beside each, because they are what distinguishes "the pass was windowed to
  each piece" from "the whole pass went to every piece" — the structural
  assertions cannot see the difference. Child 1 covers the cycle from its
  start, so its take anchor is 0; child 0 starts 24000 frames into the cycle,
  so its anchors are 24000.

  WHY IT FAILS ON main: `takes-split` REFUSES there, so pass 1 is already
  rejected. It would also fail against a silent fallback to `takes`:
  `LegacyTakes` DROPS a column starting before the pass and would never cut O
  at the cycle end, so child 2 would not exist at all and child 0 would still
  be O at its full [120000,192000) — a take extending 48000 frames beyond the
  cycle, which is the very thing X8 forbids.
-->
<SActionScript version="1" name="rec_split_cycle_inside">

  <setup project="new"/>

  <actions>
    <snap-to-grid-disable/>
    <add-track index="-1"/>

    <place-clip trackPath="0" filePath="../test_sawtooth.wav"
                timePos="120000" startOffset="0" duration="72000"/>
    <assert-clip-window clip="0,0" startTime="120000" duration="72000"
                        startOffset="0"/>

    <!-- ===================== PASS 1 ===================== -->
    <place-recording trackPath="0" filePath="../test_sawtooth.wav"
                     mode="takes-split" timePos="96000" length="48000"/>

    <assert-clip-window clip="0,0" startTime="120000" duration="24000"/>
    <assert-take-column clip="0,0" shape="direct" takes="2" activeTake="1"
                        comp=""/>
    <assert-clip-window clip="0,0" take="1" startOffset="24000"/>
    <assert-clip-window clip="0,1" startTime="96000" duration="24000"
                        startOffset="0"/>
    <assert-take-column clip="0,1" shape="none"/>
    <assert-clip-window clip="0,2" startTime="144000" duration="48000"
                        startOffset="24000"/>
    <assert-take-column clip="0,2" shape="none"/>
    <assert-clip-window clip="0,3" expectReject="true"/>

    <!-- ===================== PASS 2 ===================== -->
    <place-recording trackPath="0" filePath="../test_sawtooth.wav"
                     mode="takes-split" timePos="96000" length="48000"/>

    <!-- TWO COLUMNS, and the pass went onto BOTH of them at their own
         extents. No new child: everything inside the cycle was already
         covered, so nothing was cut and nothing was placed. -->
    <assert-clip-window clip="0,0" startTime="120000" duration="24000"/>
    <assert-take-column clip="0,0" shape="direct" takes="3" activeTake="2"
                        comp=""/>
    <assert-clip-window clip="0,0" take="2" startOffset="24000"/>
    <assert-clip-window clip="0,0" take="2" startOffset="0"
                        expectReject="true"/>

    <assert-clip-window clip="0,1" startTime="96000" duration="24000"/>
    <assert-take-column clip="0,1" shape="direct" takes="2" activeTake="1"
                        comp=""/>
    <assert-clip-window clip="0,1" take="1" startOffset="0"/>
    <assert-clip-window clip="0,1" take="1" startOffset="24000"
                        expectReject="true"/>

    <!-- NO TAKE BEYOND THE CYCLE: O's tail is still a plain clip at its own
         extent, two passes later. -->
    <assert-clip-window clip="0,2" startTime="144000" duration="48000"
                        startOffset="24000"/>
    <assert-take-column clip="0,2" shape="none"/>
    <assert-clip-window clip="0,3" expectReject="true"/>

    <!-- ONE UNDO PER PASS, back to one plain clip. -->
    <undo count="2"/>
    <assert-clip-window clip="0,0" startTime="120000" duration="72000"
                        startOffset="0"/>
    <assert-take-column clip="0,0" shape="none"/>
    <assert-clip-window clip="0,1" expectReject="true"/>
  </actions>

  <assertions>
    <assert-track-count equals="1"/>
  </assertions>

</SActionScript>
